          <p class="study-swing__lead">One pivot <i>P</i> carries two declared phase traces through the same finite arc. <i>C</i> and <i>D</i> are the turning positions; <i>K</i> is the shared projection called <strong>Sun–Moon Kiss</strong>. The second trace is displaced by the visible phase offset δ. This is a clock-and-pendulum display—not a trebuchet model, eclipse predictor or new law of time.</p>

